{"seconds": 5.180545582901686, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-extension-v1/submissions/I10/gpt-4.1-2025-04-14.json", "submission_sha256": "e454e307ce9ef555bf37c8edad01da7f28b013a689e94f33ce5a8c80e9ab1df1", "code_sha256": "2ba2a9d1f114869fc1cea6b8855237443c53e79d4c02fb2b83c9e58092b3c538", "description": "This solution builds a binary classifier to determine MRI scan acceptability based on precomputed image quality metrics (IQMs). The approach uses a pipeline with (1) train-set-only median imputation for missing values, (2) train-set-only robust scaling (median/IQR), and (3) a balanced random forest classifier (class_weight='balanced', random_state fixed, 100 trees). Cross-validation is used internally on the training set (stratified 5-fold, balanced accuracy scoring) to grid-search both max_depth and min_samples_leaf hyperparameters. No information from the test set is used beyond applying the fitted imputer/scaler. Test data is not used for statistics or model tuning. Integer predictions (0=include, 1=exclude) are returned with shape (n_test,). No identifiers, site, or label fields are used. All IQMs are treated as numeric. No tuning based on test outcomes is performed. This is a straightforward single-model solution maximizing generalizability with careful handling of missing data and class imbalance.", "code_lines": 48, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

